<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>3.2.3: Writing Linear Models without Technology</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00717</md:content-id>
    <md:title>3.2.3: Writing Linear Models without Technology</md:title>
    <md:uuid>50c74e60-ceab-4ce1-9c5a-3d5e9b8a2ec6</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <para>Linear models can also be found by hand in some situations when the data follows a linear pattern since the slope remains the same between data points. </para>
      <para>
        <emphasis>Linear Models from Tables</emphasis>
      </para>
      <para>
        <quote>
  </quote>
        <quote>For 1 - 4, use the scenario and table below:</quote>
        <quote>The table below shows the number of songs Marcus will have in his collection as he adds new songs each month.</quote>
      </para>
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <title>Activity</title>
        <exercise data-content-id="50701f9a-8db4-46eb-a7b0-673edcb2a852" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
            <para> What is the initial amount of songs, or the \(y\)-intercept of this situation? </para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! 200</para>
            <para>The correct answer is 200.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="b76d8608-acae-4296-83b1-ea0609be1338" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
            <para> What is the slope, or rate of change? </para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! 15</para>
            <para>The correct answer is 15.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <!--Q#3-->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para> Write the equation of the linear model that represents the situation in slope-intercept form. </para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>\(N = 15t + 200\)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <exercise data-content-id="487937b8-cda6-4e24-836b-d9802cb72dac" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
            <para> How many songs will Marcus have in 8 months? </para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! 320</para>
            <para> Compare your answer: 
        \(N = 15(8) + 200=320\)
        \(N = 15(8) + 200=320\)</para>
            <para>The correct answer is 320.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="c2dc9fc0-7c03-4b46-aa0b-09e5d9f9e26e" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>(Hint: Work each row backwards to where \(x= 0\).)</para>
            <para>
              <quote>For 5 - 8, use the situation and table below:</quote>
              <quote>A new plant food is introduced to a young tree to test its effect on the height of the tree. The table shows the height of the tree, H, in feet \(x\) months since measurements began.</quote>
            </para>
            <para> What is the initial height of the tree, or the \(y\)-intercept, when measurements began? </para>
            <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>The correct answer is .</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="c61b5a88-59f5-463a-af77-a760b9dcdc31" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Enter your answer here as a fraction in simplest form:</para>
            <para> What is the slope, or rate of change? </para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(\frac12\)</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(\frac12\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <!--Q#7-->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para> Write the equation of the linear model that represents the situation in slope-intercept form. </para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>\(H= \frac12 x\) +12.5\)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <exercise data-content-id="2f1f631d-86fb-4a2c-bbb4-bf2eafd59a62" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
            <para> What will the height of the tree be in 14 months? </para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! 19.5</para>
            <para> Compare your answer: 
        \(H= \frac12 (14) +12.5 =19.5\)
        \(H= \frac12 (14) +12.5 =19.5\)</para>
            <para>The correct answer is 19.5.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="10194ca5-8de5-4c66-80e3-516330af7969" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Linear Models from Graphs</para>
            <para>
              <quote>For 9 - 12, use the situation and graph below:</quote>
              <quote>The graph models the cost in dollars, \(C\), of renting a tent at a campground for n nights.
          <figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_03_04_06_01.jpg"/></media></figure></quote>
            </para>
            <para> What is the \(y\)-intercept of the graph? </para>
            <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! 30</para>
            <para>The correct answer is 30.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="04a3607e-460c-4272-bfb0-71b0d83a10b9" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
            <para> What is the slope, or rate of change? </para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! 10</para>
            <para>The correct answer is 10.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <!--Q#11-->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para> Write the equation of the linear model that represents the situation in slope-intercept form. </para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>\(C=10n + 30\)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <exercise data-content-id="18d01656-b556-4ad1-97c4-43280947ff88" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
            <para> How much does it cost to rent a tent for 5 nights? </para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para> Compare your answer: 
        \(C=10n + 30\)
        \(C=10n + 30\)
        \(C=10(5) + 30=80\)
        \(C=10(5) + 30=80\)</para>
            <para>The correct answer is .</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
    </section>
  </content>
